From 7d4377e59c088a850126a56c56266d704ca78f28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:50:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] SHTSPELL (web): MInShuttle1 / MInShuttle2 in the teach
 tables, Motion View and Home

EastSun 20260930: fix the shuttle spelling everywhere (the C++ commit of the same name renames the aliases).
- JSON/Teach-config.json, JSON/offline/Teach-config.offline.json and their JSON/js shims: the section / motor names
  MInShutte1/2 -> MInShuttle1/2 (24 each; no correct-name entry existed, so no duplicates). If these tables are
  regenerated from a teach.ini that still has the old sections, the old spelling comes back -- regenerate from this
  machine's teach.ini.
- page/Alert.MotionView.html, page/Main.MotionView.html: the in-shuttle left/right teach points read [MInShuttle1] first,
  [MInShutte1] as the fallback (this machine's teach.ini has only MInShuttle1, so the pages were showing the hard-coded
  defaults).
- page/HW.home.html: the two static labels "[M11] MInShuttle1", "[M12] MInShuttle2".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
